7. Character Generation Testing
The character-generation module should be tested for:
•	Correct character names
•	Character roles
•	Personality
•	Appearance
•	Relationships
•	Character uniqueness
•	Consistency with the generated story
Example
Input:
"A young detective investigates a mysterious disappearance."
Expected characters:
•	Detective
•	Missing person
•	Supporting character
•	Possible antagonist
The generated characters should be relevant to the story.
________________________________________
8. Character Consistency Testing
Character consistency is particularly important for AI-generated comics.
Test scenario
Generate five panels containing the same character.
Verify:
•	Name remains unchanged.
•	Age remains consistent.
•	Clothing description remains reasonably consistent.
•	Physical characteristics remain consistent.
•	Personality remains consistent.
•	Character role does not unexpectedly change.
Panel 1 ──┐
Panel 2 ──┤
Panel 3 ──┼──► Character Consistency Check
Panel 4 ──┤
Panel 5 ──┘
________________________________________
9. Scene Generation Testing
Verify that generated scenes:
•	Follow the story.
•	Have appropriate locations.
•	Contain relevant characters.
•	Maintain chronological order.
•	Connect logically to previous scenes.
Example
Scene 1 → Character discovers robot
Scene 2 → Character activates robot
Scene 3 → Robot reveals its secret
The sequence should not unexpectedly reverse or contradict the story.
________________________________________
