11. Dialogue Testing
Test whether dialogue:
•	Matches the character.
•	Relates to the current scene.
•	Is grammatically reasonable.
•	Does not contradict the story.
•	Is suitable for the selected tone.
•	Is not unnecessarily repetitive.
Example
If a character is described as a scientist, dialogue should generally reflect the context and personality established for that character.
