25. Acceptance Criteria
ComicCraft can be considered ready for release when:
•	Users can register and log in.
•	Users can create comic projects.
•	A story can be generated from a prompt.
•	Characters and scenes can be generated.
•	Stories can be divided into panels.
•	Dialogue can be generated and edited.
•	Users can modify generated content.
•	Projects can be saved and reopened.
•	Generated artwork can be displayed when the visual pipeline is enabled.
•	The final comic can be previewed and exported.
•	Major security and functional tests pass.
•	Critical defects are resolved.
